    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1064-a6">

                <pb facs="1155" n="1059" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1059"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6 in No. 267.]</seg><lb/><dateline
                        rendition="#center">[Telegraphic reply thereto <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-02-17">February 17, 1898</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">His Royal Highness the <hi rendition="#small-caps">Duke of
                        Connaught, K. G.</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Bagshot:</hi></p>
                <p>I beg to express to your royal highness my most sincere thanks for your telegram
                    of sympathy with my country and its Navy in the loss of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Maine</hi> under such appalling circumstances. I
                    immediately cabled your sympathetic message to my Government. The ambassador is
                    in Egypt.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
